---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Impact — Spatialytics"
  description="How Spatialytics aims to create high-wage tech roles, reduce business overhead, and keep value in Greater Minnesota."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-narrow">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16">
        <p class="text-cyan-400 font-medium mb-3 text-sm uppercase tracking-wide">Impact</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6 leading-tight">
          Closing the software industry gap in Greater Minnesota
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
          The Brainerd Lakes area has strong healthcare, retail, tourism, and trades — and a clear underrepresentation of software product companies and computer & mathematical occupations. Spatialytics is built to change that equation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-5 mb-20">
        <div class="card text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-cyan-400 mb-1">~1.1%</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Computer & Math occupations in Northwest MN</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-cyan-400 mb-1">~3.5%</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Statewide average</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-amber-400 mb-1">~$62k</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Family COL (2+1) Northwest MN</div>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-center">
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-amber-400 mb-1">~$82k</div>
          <div class="text-xs text-slate-400">Family COL (2+1) Twin Cities</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mb-20">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold mb-10">How we create impact</h2>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
          <div class="card">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-5 text-cyan-400 text-xl font-bold">1</div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">High-wage work that stays</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Software product development, spatial platforms, and SaaS create roles that are less seasonal than tourism and higher-wage than many local service jobs. Keeping that work in the region matters.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-5 text-cyan-400 text-xl font-bold">2</div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Tools that reduce overhead</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Local print shops, small manufacturers, and service businesses often run on fragmented systems. Better software frees capacity and can support stronger wages and retention.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-cyan-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-5 text-cyan-400 text-xl font-bold">3</div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-3">Pathways for local talent</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              CLC and other regional programs produce graduates in computer-related, design, natural resources, and business fields. More local product companies give them a reason to build careers here.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card border-cyan-500/30 mb-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">The industry gap is real</h2>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Northwest Minnesota employs roughly 2,400 people in Computer & Mathematical occupations — about 1.1% of regional employment. Statewide the share is closer to 3.4–3.7%, with the Twin Cities holding the large majority of those roles.
        </p>
        <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Local government and utilities have internal GIS and IT roles. Independent software product companies and spatial-analytics startups headquartered in the Brainerd Lakes area are rare. That is the gap Spatialytics is designed to help fill.
        </p>
        <a href="/compare" class="btn-secondary text-sm">Full regional comparison →</a>
      </div>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 mb-16 items-center">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Talent retention starts with opportunity</h2>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            When high-wage software and spatial roles are scarce locally, talent leaves or never returns. Building product companies in the region is one of the most direct ways to change that pattern.
          </p>
          <p class="text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Spatialytics is intentionally structured so that growth in the business can translate into year-round roles and mentorship pathways connected to local education programs.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card bg-slate-900/80">
          <h3 class="font-semibold mb-4">Aligned with regional goals</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-300">
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-400">→</span> Diversify beyond seasonal tourism and retail</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-400">→</span> Grow higher-wage employment</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-400">→</span> Support local business competitiveness</li>
            <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-cyan-400">→</span> Keep CLC and regional graduates in the area</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="text-center">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn-primary text-lg">Partner with us</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
